{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:40:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_df20977a884a494a8a61150159f9f604","id":"pg_4ea07297285253fab3c8c56bad24a227","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sudoprivacy-sudocode-changes-md-a67bb90f5c4b-c56bad24a227.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_8d0f7011430c5a81980d57e482fedeb7"],"title":"sudoprivacy/sudocode/CHANGES.md @ a67bb90f5c4b","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:40:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df20977a884a494a8a61150159f9f604"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_04d08ece3e59789e2123736bd0be72b93e3aa34ff53d91a6b01a689cfe1e4ad7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"scode speaks the Agent Communication Protocol natively over two transports sharing one handler chain: `scode acp` over stdio and `scode acp serve --port N` over WebSocket."},{"claim_ids":["clm_08645cf940261c73a8ca3456e070460e7304f72a72951d88369390f182ee166f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions persist as JSONL under `<cwd>/.scode/sessions/<workspace-fingerprint>/`; session/load restores transcript, model, compaction state and fork lineage, but not permission-mode overrides, background commands, or MCP servers not passed in the request."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2b6ad02d2676386c1605fc8e4caefab386d742f10aa740c46abf7fe901633200"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Automatic compaction trims oversized tool text (over 8,192 code points) to a head/tail with marker before running a checkpoint pipeline; successful replacement archives the original transcript as `<transcript>.before-compact-<timestamp>`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2ccf0cc1810d8b21b293ba31acfef57dc1cd325ffc4097959cfd7e39aed03dca"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The WebSocket server exposes JSON-RPC at ws://localhost:8080/ws plus an embedded interactive Web UI at http://localhost:8080/; both transports share streaming, tool use, elicitation and permission prompting."},{"claim_ids":["clm_417cdff9cb1fb7401495ead4fb2d106bb82922ce1beaf903f85af3be8fbe5b6d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A session/prompt starting with `/` runs as a slash command (e.g. /help, /status, /cost, /model, /compact, /diff, /doctor), and the agent advertises the command table via a session/update notification after session/new or session/load."},{"claim_ids":["clm_691a52f2580adc08639655701c876431c5dfc948220c486c9175eb04fba15791"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per-session memory is controlled via `_meta.sudocode.memory`; 'disabled' means the session neither reads nor writes the persistent memory directory, and disabling never deletes existing entries."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b502023c83300e2516d2a13d7084bab111158fc3a64c1a2a1e6ac27308de8618"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Forking via `session/new` with `_meta.sudocode.forkFrom` copies the source transcript into a new first-class session under the new cwd; the source is read, never modified, and the initialize response advertises sessionFork for feature detection."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c12ebc788c4fab2c9191876d5b65f2fdd3723ad1837703a063e03cbc4c81d403"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"ACP sessions accept `_meta.sudocode.systemPrompt` (replaces built-in static system-prompt blocks) and `appendSystemPrompt` (appended after them); non-string or empty values are rejected with invalid_params (-32602)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_04d08ece3e59789e2123736bd0be72b93e3aa34ff53d91a6b01a689cfe1e4ad7","clm_08645cf940261c73a8ca3456e070460e7304f72a72951d88369390f182ee166f","clm_2b6ad02d2676386c1605fc8e4caefab386d742f10aa740c46abf7fe901633200","clm_2ccf0cc1810d8b21b293ba31acfef57dc1cd325ffc4097959cfd7e39aed03dca","clm_417cdff9cb1fb7401495ead4fb2d106bb82922ce1beaf903f85af3be8fbe5b6d","clm_691a52f2580adc08639655701c876431c5dfc948220c486c9175eb04fba15791","clm_b502023c83300e2516d2a13d7084bab111158fc3a64c1a2a1e6ac27308de8618","clm_c12ebc788c4fab2c9191876d5b65f2fdd3723ad1837703a063e03cbc4c81d403"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:40:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_df20977a884a494a8a61150159f9f604","id":"pg_65a0ca1c853c51409ed8546bc1f1734d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sudoprivacy-sudocode-docs-acp-md-a67bb90f5c4b-546bc1f1734d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_b91a8fc98a015822b63b5babccdb5ccc"],"title":"sudoprivacy/sudocode/docs/acp.md @ a67bb90f5c4b","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:40:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df20977a884a494a8a61150159f9f604"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_80a98ef88606fed64048f87c211ad90e4cd57298bde92d2733167287334378b1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Authentication supports three modes — subscription (CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN), proxy (PROXY_AUTH_TOKEN + PROXY_BASE_URL), and api-key (Anthropic, OpenAI, xAI, Gemini, DashScope keys) — with auto-detection in that order."}],"claim_ids":["clm_80a98ef88606fed64048f87c211ad90e4cd57298bde92d2733167287334378b1"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:40:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_df20977a884a494a8a61150159f9f604","id":"pg_9713536c0791577799b269b0f6098e8d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sudoprivacy-sudocode-docs-authentication-md-a67bb90f5c4b-69b0f6098e8d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_5d4e89750e125dbeaa6e4b50435091ec"],"title":"sudoprivacy/sudocode/docs/authentication.md @ a67bb90f5c4b","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:40:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df20977a884a494a8a61150159f9f604"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_6c84ee8add798f08a7ed95ba56f65344fd49176ca2362cb12c366dbcadea80c4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sudo Code positions itself as an agent unit, not an orchestrator: it plugs into a nexus-VFS `chat-with-me` mailbox primitive so humans, orchestrators, or peer agents over ACP can drive it."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c70c1ca32d78f554c24a1a2ad80cb4101849d6686668fe0a8ad47c9895a27d56"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"One scode binary serves copilot, worker, or standalone roles depending on the FsBackend implementation: StdFsBackend (host std::fs), NexusVfsFsBackend (gRPC to remote kernel), or KernelFsBackend (in-process syscalls)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f7c23209a3ab0f22735ca3e247b046d219f653cb2cd8c0dadf75f4ba8787cd7d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project commits to inline-only terminal output (no alternate-screen TUI, no ratatui), local-first operation with zero telemetry by default, and semver stability with no forced auto-updates."}],"claim_ids":["clm_6c84ee8add798f08a7ed95ba56f65344fd49176ca2362cb12c366dbcadea80c4","clm_c70c1ca32d78f554c24a1a2ad80cb4101849d6686668fe0a8ad47c9895a27d56","clm_f7c23209a3ab0f22735ca3e247b046d219f653cb2cd8c0dadf75f4ba8787cd7d"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:40:28Z","created_by_operation":"op_df20977a884a494a8a61150159f9f604","id":"pg_bbc4f99d2d82532483696205a64ea783","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/sudoprivacy-sudocode-readme-md-a67bb90f5c4b-6205a64ea783.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f26e4333dde05645a1d409ce68f0408b"],"title":"sudoprivacy/sudocode/README.md @ a67bb90f5c4b","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:40:28Z","updated_by_operation":"op_df20977a884a494a8a61150159f9f604"}
